# Source recordings — keep the originals locally, commit only the web encodes.
# wiki-graph.mp4 is 13.7MB; wiki-graph-loop.mp4 is 0.5MB and looks the same
# at the size it's displayed. Git keeps every version of a binary forever,
# so large sources bloat the clone permanently.
assets/*-source.*
assets/wiki-graph.mp4

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Internal architecture draft. Contains unresolved commercial and technical
# questions written for me, not for a client or an employer. GitHub Pages
# serves everything that gets committed, so keeping it out of the repo is the
# only thing that actually keeps it private — noindex and an unlinked URL
# don't. Delete this line when it's ready to be public.
notes/architecture/

# Learning artifacts. Same reasoning as above — these contain my commercial
# reading of the research, not just the research. The wiki they're built from
# (claude-rollout/) IS committed, because it's synthesis of public material.
# Delete this line to publish them.
explainers/
